  27:     - Each sprite instance is a scaled copy of one of the two prototypes, placed on the grid.
  28: 
  29:     Rule:
  30:     - Identify the two prototype patterns from the smallest-area sprites.
  31:     - For each sprite, determine which prototype it matches and its integer scale factor.
  32:     - Replace it with the other prototype at the same scale, aligned by an internal anchor region (color-1 pixels).
  33: 
  34:     Key insight: Every sprite toggles to the alternate prototype; the anchor sub-region inside each sprite pins the alignment so swapped sprites land in the correct position regardless of scale.
  35:     """
